data.reasoningText:
Perfect! Now I can see that the scaffold imports the oxide skins directly:
```
import "tinymce/skins/ui/oxide/skin.css";
import "tinymce/skins/ui/oxide/content.css";
import "tinymce/skins/content/default/content.css";
```

So the oxide module is distributed as part of the tinymce npm package. Now I have a good understanding of what needs to be done. Let me create a comprehensive summary of findings.

Let me verify one more thing - let me check if there are any existing CSS build patterns to understand how to generate a skin CSS.

